    <string name="about_text">This application is a clean-room reimplementation of the Privacy Friendly Password Generator. Sourcecode licensed under GPLv3.</string>
    <string name="more_info">More information can be found on:</string>
    <string name="tutorial_slide_1_title">Welcome!</string>
    <string name="tutorial_slide_1_body">With this Password Generator you can generate different passwords for all your accounts while remembering only one master password.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_slide_2_title">Generate passwords</string>
    <string name="tutorial_slide_2_body">Choose an account from the list. Invent a master password as your initial secret. Based on this master password all other passwords are generated. Copy the generated password to the website or service.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_slide_3_title">Accounts</string>
    <string name="tutorial_slide_3_body">Website providers often use password composition policies. These policies might force us to create passwords with special characteristics like a minimum length. Characteristics of a password can be set in the account.</string>
    <string name="masterpw_tutorial_slide_1_title">Master Password</string>
    <string name="masterpw_tutorial_slide_1_body">The master password is the only password, that you have to remember. Based on it all other passwords are generated. The master password is not stored in the application. If you lose it you have to reset all your passwords.</string>
    <string name="masterpw_tutorial_slide_2_title">Master Password Tips</string>
    <string name="masterpw_tutorial_slide_2_body">Do not include personal data (like birthdays). Do not use character sequences from the keyboard. Try to make it as long as possible for you.</string>
    <string name="empty_list_hint">No accounts yet. Tap + to add one.</string>
